# Build context hygiene. Two reasons this file matters beyond speed:
#
#   - .env / .env.local would otherwise be baked into the image. The web build
#     reads .env.local and it would override the build args the deployment
#     passes in, silently pointing a production image at localhost.
#   - Copying host node_modules over a Linux image brings platform-specific
#     native builds with it (argon2, next-swc), which fail at runtime in ways
#     that look nothing like the cause.

**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/release
**/.turbo
**/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets and local overrides.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

.git
.github
**/*.log
**/coverage

# Native shells are never part of a server image.
apps/desktop
apps/mobile
docs
deploy/backups*
